    <div class="story-content">
      <h2>Pedagogical Background & Vision</h2>
      <p>
        Master Manikant Yadav is an educator, educational technologist, and mathematician based in Supaul, Bihar. Having completed his B.Sc in Mathematics from BNMU and B.Ed from Jiwaji University, followed by qualifying the prestigious Bihar STET 2025 examination with 107 marks, Manikant combines mathematical precision with linguistics.
      </p>

      <h2>The Sentence Logic Model</h2>
      <p>
        Recognizing that rote learning fails students when facing complex translation, Master Manikant pioneered the <strong>Sentence Logic Framework</strong>. This model breaks down English sentence structure into algorithmic steps:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Formula Identification:</strong> Mapping Hindi tense markers to exact auxiliary verb matrices.</li>
        <li><strong>Structural Inversion:</strong> Seamlessly swapping Hindi's SOV (Subject + Object + Verb) order into English's SVO (Subject + Verb + Object) order.</li>
        <li><strong>Zero Ratta Practice:</strong> Building intuition through thousands of contextual drill examples.</li>
      </ul>

